<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>bundleid</key>
	<string>com.worktree-studio.alfred</string>
	<key>name</key>
	<string>Worktree Studio</string>
	<key>description</key>
	<string>Jump to a session, worktree or dev server without leaving the keyboard.</string>
	<key>createdby</key>
	<string>Worktree Studio</string>
	<key>webaddress</key>
	<string>https://github.com/dovid-rosenberg/worktree-studio</string>
	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `wt` to list your active Claude sessions first, then every worktree.

  ⏎  open in your editor
  ⌘  reveal in Finder
  ⌃  start the dev server (a session starts its whole feature stack)
  ⌥  stop it — or, on a session that came from a ticket, open the ticket
  ⇧  open the Worktree Studio cockpit

Needs Worktree Studio running on 127.0.0.1:7788 (or whatever web.port in
~/.config/worktree-studio/config.json says), plus jq. Nothing to configure:
the workflow reads the same config file and API token the app itself uses.</string>
	<key>disabled</key>
	<false/>
	<key>version</key>
	<string>1.0</string>
	<key>variables</key>
	<dict/>
	<key>variablesdontexport</key>
	<array/>
	<key>connections</key>
	<dict>
		<key>F1LTER00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001</key>
		<array>
			<!-- One destination, five entries: Alfred routes a modified return along
			     the connection whose bitmask matches, so every modifier the Script
			     Filter's `mods` block defines needs its own line here or the press
			     falls through and does the unmodified thing instead. -->
			<dict>
				<key>destinationuid</key>
				<string>ACT10N00-0000-4000-8000-000000000002</string>
				<key>modifiers</key>
				<integer>0</integer>
